Spoiler alert.  Please do not read if you don't wish to become spoiled.

Since the tournament I have decided to go back and finish all of the
Nethack character types.  Only two remained until today, Healer and
Barbarian.  I can cross Healer off the list now.  Barbarian should be
relatively simple.

I had never played Healers before because, well, they're not very
exciting.  But now that I've finished one, I'd say it's probably the
most challenging and possibly the most "fun" character.  You do not
have access to very many powerful offensive spells or weapons.  Until
you get the Staff that is.  But even then, it's best to play
defensively with a Healer.

I also chose to play a Gnome, just for the variety.  I use the
spoilers, but not for the Quests, so I didn't know exactly what to
expect.  Of course I had heard of the famous Staff of Misspelling, but
I didn't realize how powerful it really is.

My first promising character died very quickly at the hands of the
Cyclops.  The difficulty in fighting him while he has the Staff
presents a real challenge.  Obtaining level-drain resistance before the
quest pretty much dictates doing the Castle first.  In my case I went a
little further, just to get a Robe from the Valley priest, as I had not
previously had access to one.  My second strategy was to increase my
spellcasting ability. I happened to find a +3 Helm of Brilliance early
in the game, which helped immeasurably.

My personal strategy was use use polymorph/control to become a vampire
lord, then charm most of the Dragons around the Cyclops.  Using this
strategy it was pretty easy to beat him.  I would be interested in
hearing other strategies.  My other idea would be to somehow get
Stormbringer, but I didn't want to waste a wish on a chaotic weapon.

Greg.



